From ac9a5973e8eec0929030820a177eb37859344efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rpiios <grinkod.bogdan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ board (RASPBERRYPI3)

The Pi target is the HD2 iOS 7 kernel with a different board layer: it
builds with BOARD_CONFIG_QSD8250_LEO so every iOS 7 compatibility change
stays on, and HD2 hardware files are excluded with BOARD_CONFIG_RASPBERRYPI3.

- pexpert/arm/pe_rpi3.c: platform expert with the HD2 PE's exported API
  (stages, fatal/panic screens, display present into the firmware
  framebuffer, 320x533 -> 480x800 scaling), optional PL011 output.
- pexpert/arm/rpi3_timer.c: armctrl IRQ + 1 MHz system timer compare 3.
- osfmk/arm/locore.s: early identity maps for the framebuffer and UART.
- IOS7Rpi3SD.cpp + rpi3_sd.c: SDHCI (Arasan) SD card, GPIO48-53 -> ALT3;
  class keeps the IOS7LeoSDCC2 name the root-file/logger drivers match.
- IOS7Rpi3Input.cpp: placeholder until the USB mouse transport.
- Cortex-A53 CPU id; 'brcm,bcm2837' platform match.
